WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.360
"Plant-Based Diets Could Save Millions of
Lives and Trillions of Dollars a Year"

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.080
Based on a meta-analysis
of studies following

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:12.640
millions of people
and their diets for years,

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:15.360
better adherence
to more plant-based diets,

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.160
especially ones emphasizing
healthy plant foods,

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.160
is beneficial
for lowering the risks

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.080
of major chronic conditions,

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.880
including type 2 diabetes,
cardiovascular disease,

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:25.680
and cancer,

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.920
as well as premature death
in general.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.200
Moving to diets with
fewer animal-sourced foods

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.280
could end up saving the lives of
millions of people every year,

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.640
in addition to saving
trillions of dollars.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:42.960
Here’s how many lives might be
saved by a healthy global diet,

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:44.240
which is like more of

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:46.560
a Mediterranean cut-down-on-red
meat-and-sugar,

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:48.480
eat-lots-of-fruits-
and-vegetables diet,

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.560
versus a vegetarian diet,

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:52.240
versus a vegan diet.

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.360
So, we’re talking
major health benefits

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.440
eating fewer
animal-sourced foods:

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:00.880
Healthier diets could save
five million lives a year.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:02.880
If the world went vegetarian,

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.520
we’d save seven million lives
a year,

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.280
and if the world
started eating vegan,

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.960
we might save eight million
lives per year.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:14.960
So, the question is less "what
to do" and more "how to do it."

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:18.400
In other words, the main problem
is the implementation gap,

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:21.040
which is likely a result
of things like inertia,

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:23.520
individual addictions,
commercial interests,

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:25.120
and economic issues.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:28.240
For example, why did
the World Health Organization

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:31.280
pull support from a global
initiative promoting

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:33.120
more plant-based foods?

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:36.240
Yeah, eating that way might save
millions of lives,

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.160
but a global move to such a diet

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.640
could lead to the loss
of millions of jobs

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:42.560
linked to animal agriculture.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:45.040
"’[T]he total
or nearly total elimination

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:48.160
of foods of animal origin
would destroy cattle farming

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:49.440
and many other activities

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:52.320
related to the production
of meat and dairy products."

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:54.800
"The initiative ’urging
for a centralized control

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.560
of our dietary choices’

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:00.400
risked ’the total elimination of
consumers’ freedom of choice."

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:03.280
And that was the reaction
to just recommending

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:06.080
people try eating
more plant-based.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:08.160
And hey,
that’s just meat and dairy.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:11.280
Think of how many jobs in
the candy and liquor industries

00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:13.120
would be lost if people
all of a sudden decided

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:14.480
to eat and drink healthier.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:17.200
It could have
drastic consequences.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:20.000
There is a reason
that soda companies sponsor

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.000
major health organizations.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.200
Over a five-year period,

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.400
researchers found that the
Coca-Cola Company and PepsiCo

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.760
sponsored "a total of 96
national health organizations

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:31.360
in United States,

00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:34.000
including many medical
and public health institutions

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:38.640
whose specific missions include
fighting the obesity epidemic."

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:42.560
The American Academy of Family
Physicians took their money,

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:46.080
the American Academy
of Pediatrics, the AMA,

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:47.360
the dietitians,

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:50.960
the Society
for Nutrition Educators.

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:53.600
Maybe the soda companies
genuinely care

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:55.440
about the public’s health?

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.160
Hardly.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:57.360
During the same study period,

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.400
those same two corporations
lobbied against

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.360
29 public health bills intended
to reduce soda consumption

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:05.760
or improve nutrition.

00:03:05.760 --> 00:03:08.400
Although national food
guidelines are designed,

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.200
ostensibly, to translate
scientific evidence

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.400
with respect to food,
dietary patterns, and health,

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.880
their development
has increasingly become

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:19.040
a corporate
and political process

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:21.280
as much as scientific one,

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:23.920
often with corporate
and political influences

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:26.240
overriding the science.

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:27.920
As I detailed before,

00:03:27.920 --> 00:03:31.200
this goes back all the way
to the first edition

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:32.720
of the American food goals

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:35.440
which started out
strongly recommending

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.360
decreasing our intake of meat,
dairy, and eggs

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:38.640
to reduce saturated fat,

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:41.200
as well as reducing
salt and sugar intake.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:43.840
However, lobbyists
reacted vehemently

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:46.880
and succeeded in having the
wording in the report changed

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:50.080
to "increase the consumption
of lean meat."

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:51.360
Thus, the year in which

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.280
protecting public health
in the United States

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:56.880
became secondary to protecting
corporate health and wealth

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:59.360
was 1977.

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:01.520
Now, nearly 50 years later,

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:04.160
the efforts of the dietary
guidelines advisory committee

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:06.560
is recognized
for all the work they do,

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.240
but despite these achievements,

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:10.480
some key recommendations
in the current guidelines

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:12.560
do not reflect
the best available evidence

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:15.040
that "strongly support shifting

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:17.760
toward lower consumption
of animal protein sources

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:20.720
and higher intakes
of healthy plant sources."

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:23.280
But it’s such a politically
hot-button issue

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:25.600
that even when it comes
to the worst of the worst--

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.840
processed meats,
like bacon, ham, hot dogs,

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:29.120
lunch meat, and sausage--

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:32.080
known to cause cancer
in human beings,

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:34.240
yet all we have are provisos

00:04:34.240 --> 00:04:39.520
"to consume these carcinogenic
foods ’in moderation.’"

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:43.440
Given that there may be no safe
limit for alcohol consumption,

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:45.040
the Canadian guidelines advise

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:48.000
no more than
one to two drinks a week.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.760
Its dietary guidelines
were updated

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.520
to emphasize
the importance of consuming

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:52.560
more plant-based products,

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.600
and even removed dairy
as its own food group.

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:57.200
How were the Canadians so free

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:59.520
to be able
to better follow the evidence?

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:02.560
They decided to remove
industry-funded studies

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:04.400
from their consideration.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.240
What a concept.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:10.080
If we were going to try
to stick to the best science,

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.040
the eating pattern that is
healthiest for humans,

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:16.160
the one that best reduces
the risk of our leading killers,

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:19.760
would be a diet centered
around whole plant foods.

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:20.800
The reason we don’t see this

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:22.720
in national food guide
recommendations

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:25.440
can be explained by factors
other than science,

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:27.120
specifically,
corporate interests

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:29.440
reflected in heavily
government-subsidized

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:30.320
animal-sourced products

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:34.080
and the political might of the
ultra-processed food industry.

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:36.000
A whole food, plant-based diet

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.320
might be considered
the dietary gold standard

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:41.520
against which other dietary
patterns could be compared,

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:42.960
if for no other reason

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:45.200
than it’s the only diet
that has been shown

00:05:45.200 --> 00:05:46.560
to reliably reverse

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:49.600
the progression
of coronary atherosclerosis,

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:52.160
the number-one killer
of men and women.

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:53.760
What else do we need?

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:56.720
So, if we wanted an unbiased,

00:05:56.720 --> 00:05:59.760
evidence-based
Universal Food Guide,

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:02.400
if might look
a little something like this.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:07.680
And for those of you thinking,
hey, that looks kinda familiar,

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:10.720
that’s because
it’s the Daily Dozen.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:11.360
So, you can use

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:13.600
the free
Dr. Greger’s Daily Dozen app

00:06:13.600 --> 00:06:16.720
as a reminder to fit some of
the healthiest of healthy foods

00:06:16.720 --> 00:06:19.405
into your daily routine.

